{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-355240",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(0,3),$ so ${max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=3$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=0,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(4,-2),$ so ${min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=-2$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
